      "traceTextDiagram": "Task Creation Flow (skills/todo/main.go)\n├── run() skill entrypoint \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:251\n│   └── switch case \"add\" \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:283\n│       └── handleAdd() call \u003c-- 1a\n│           ├── validateText() checks \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:587\n│           ├── store.ListByWorkspace() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:598\n│           ├── findOpenDuplicateTask() \u003c-- 1b\n│           │   └── normalizeTaskTitle() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:617\n│           ├── if duplicate exists \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:622\n│           │   └── store.Update() merge \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:643\n│           └── else create new\n│               ├── store.Add() \u003c-- 1c\n│               │   └── SQLite INSERT \u003c-- 1d\n│               ├── createTaskDependencyEdges() \u003c-- 1e\n│               │   └── graph.UpsertNode/Edge() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:2053\n│               └── return to run()\n└── persistPageRanks() \u003c-- 1f\n    ├── tasksgraph.Analyze() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:2012\n    └── store.SetPageRanks() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:2024",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen users create tasks in agentctl, the system needs to prevent duplicates, maintain task relationships (parent-child hierarchies and dependencies), and keep graph metrics up-to-date for intelligent prioritization. Without duplicate detection, users would accumulate redundant tasks across sessions. Without graph tracking, the system couldn't recommend which tasks to work on next based on their importance in the dependency network.\n\n## Details\n\n### Task Creation Entry Point\n\nThe `todo/manage` skill handles task operations through a unified interface [1a]. When `operation=\"add\"` is specified, the request flows to `handleAdd()`, which orchestrates validation, duplicate checking, persistence, and graph updates.\n\n### Duplicate Detection\n\nBefore creating a task, the system **normalizes the title** (lowercases, collapses whitespace) and searches for existing open tasks with the same normalized title, parent, and session [1b]. This prevents users from accidentally creating \"Fix bug in parser\" multiple times. If a duplicate exists, the system merges new information (description, scope path, dependencies) into the existing task rather than creating a new one.\n\n### SQLite Persistence\n\nNew tasks are inserted into the `tasks` table with a comprehensive schema [1c, 1d] that includes:\n- Core fields: title, description, status, timestamps\n- Hierarchy: `parent_id`, `children` (JSON array)\n- Dependencies: `depends_on` (JSON array of task IDs)\n- Review gate: `last_review_status`, `last_review_at`, `last_review_id`\n- Session tracking: `session_id` for multi-session continuity\n- Graph metrics: `pagerank` for prioritization\n\n### Graph Edge Creation\n\nAfter persisting the task, the system creates **structural edges** in a separate graph store [1e]. Two edge types are created:\n- `parent_of`: from parent task to child task\n- `depends_on`: from task to each of its dependencies\n\nThese edges have **no TTL** (they don't expire) because they represent permanent task relationships, unlike temporal activity edges.\n\n### PageRank Computation\n\nFinally, the system recomputes **PageRank scores** for all tasks in the workspace [1f]. This uses the gonum library to run the PageRank algorithm on the dependency graph, treating tasks as nodes and dependencies as edges. Higher PageRank scores indicate tasks that are more \"central\" or \"important\" in the dependency network—these are the tasks that many other tasks depend on, directly or indirectly. The scores are persisted back to the `pagerank` column in the tasks table for use in recommendations and prioritization."
    },
