      "traceTextDiagram": "Task Completion Flow (todo/manage skill)\n├── run() switch on operation=\"complete\" \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:316\n│   └── handleComplete() call \u003c-- 2a\n│       ├── store.Get() - fetch task \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:793\n│       ├── Dependency validation loop \u003c-- 2b\n│       │   └── check each dep.Status == done \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:819\n│       ├── Review gate enforcement \u003c-- 2c\n│       │   ├── isReviewGateEnabled() check \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:828\n│       │   ├── verify StatusReadyForReview \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:829\n│       │   └── verify LastReviewStatus == OK \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:832\n│       ├── Status \u0026 timestamp update \u003c-- 2d\n│       │   ├── task.Status = statusDone \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:838\n│       │   └── task.CompletedAt = \u0026now \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:839\n│       └── store.Update() persist \u003c-- 2e\n└── persistPageRanks() recalculation \u003c-- 2f\n    ├── store.ListByWorkspace() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:2002\n    ├── tasksgraph.Analyze() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:2012\n    └── store.SetPageRanks() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:2024",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen a user marks a task as complete, the system must ensure **data integrity** and **workflow correctness** before allowing the transition. Specifically, it must verify that all dependency tasks are finished (you can't complete a task if it depends on incomplete work), and if the workspace has a **review gate** enabled, it must enforce that the task has passed review before being marked done. This prevents premature completion and maintains quality standards.\n\n## Details\n\n### Completion Request Flow\n\nThe completion flow begins when `handleComplete()` [2a] is invoked from the main skill dispatcher. The first step is fetching the task from the database to validate it exists and belongs to the correct workspace.\n\n### Dependency Validation\n\nBefore allowing completion, the system iterates through all tasks listed in `DependsOn` [2b] and checks that each dependency has `Status == \"completed\"`. If any dependency is incomplete, the operation fails with a validation error. This ensures **topological correctness** in the task graph—you can't finish work that depends on unfinished prerequisites.\n\n### Review Gate Enforcement\n\nIf the workspace has review gates enabled (controlled by `AGENTCTL_TODO_REVIEW_GATE` environment variable), the system enforces a **quality checkpoint** [2c]. The task must be in `ready_for_review` status and have `LastReviewStatus == \"ok\"` with a valid `LastReviewID`. This prevents tasks from being marked complete without passing automated checks (lint, tests) or human review. The review gate is **kernel-owned**—agents cannot bypass it.\n\n### Status Transition\n\nOnce all validations pass, the task transitions to completed state [2d]: `Status` becomes `\"completed\"` and `CompletedAt` timestamp is set. This is persisted to SQLite [2e] via `store.Update()`, which executes an UPDATE statement on the tasks table.\n\n### Graph Recalculation\n\nAfter completion, the system recomputes **PageRank scores** [2f] for all tasks in the workspace. Completion changes the graph structure (completed tasks effectively become sinks), so PageRank values must be recalculated to maintain accurate priority rankings. This involves fetching all workspace tasks, running the tasksgraph analyzer (which uses gonum's PageRank algorithm), and bulk-updating the `pagerank` column in the database."
    },
