        {
          "id": "3f",
          "path": "/Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 533,
          "lineContent": "_, err = s.db.ExecContext(ctx, `\nINSERT INTO active_tasks (workspace_id, task_id) VALUES (?, ?)\nON CONFLICT(workspace_id) DO UPDATE SET task_id = excluded.task_id`, workspaceID, taskID)",
          "title": "Active task upsert",
          "description": "SQLite upsert ensures only one active task per workspace"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Active Task Management Flow\n├── todo/manage skill entrypoint \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/todo/main.go:251\n│   └── case \"ensure_active\" \u003c-- 3a\n│       └── store.EnsureActive() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:553\n│           ├── GetActive() check \u003c-- 3b\n│           │   └── SQL JOIN query \u003c-- 3c\n│           │       └── tasks ⋈ active_tasks\n│           ├── if not found: \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:560\n│           │   ├── Add() new task \u003c-- 3d\n│           │   └── SetActive() \u003c-- 3e\n│           │       └── UPSERT active_tasks \u003c-- 3f\n│           └── return (task, created) \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:579",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen working on tasks in agentctl, you need a way to track **which task is currently being worked on** in a given workspace. Without this, agents and users would have to manually specify the task ID for every operation, and there would be no clear answer to \"what am I working on right now?\"\n\nThe **active task** concept solves this by maintaining a single \"current task\" per workspace. This enables operations like \"add notes to the current task\" or \"complete what I'm working on\" without requiring explicit task IDs every time.\n\n## Details\n\n### Storage Model\n\nActive task state is stored in a dedicated `active_tasks` table [3f] with a **one-to-one relationship** between workspace and active task. The table uses `workspace_id` as the primary key, ensuring only one task can be active per workspace at a time.\n\n### EnsureActive Pattern\n\nThe `EnsureActive` operation [3a] implements a **get-or-create** pattern that's particularly useful for workflows that need to guarantee an active task exists:\n\n1. **First, check** if an active task already exists via a JOIN query between `tasks` and `active_tasks` tables [3c]\n2. **If found**, return it immediately with `created=false` [3b]\n3. **If not found**, create a new task with the provided default title and scope [3d], then mark it as active [3e]\n\nThis pattern is atomic and prevents race conditions through SQLite's `ON CONFLICT` upsert semantics [3f].\n\n### Setting Active Tasks\n\nThe `SetActive` operation uses an **upsert** (INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE) to atomically replace the active task [3f]. This ensures that even concurrent calls will result in a consistent final state - exactly one active task per workspace.\n\n### Use Cases\n\n- **Session restoration**: When resuming work, ensure there's an active task to attach operations to\n- **Implicit context**: Skills can operate on \"the current task\" without requiring task IDs in every call\n- **Workflow continuity**: Agents can maintain focus on a single task across multiple operations"
    },
